<title>GERMANY: Dywidag to pay nine dm dividend for 96.</title>
<headline>Dywidag to pay nine dm dividend for 96.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction firm Dyckerhoff and Widmann AG said on Friday it would pay a dividend of nine marks on its 1996 results, compared to a 10 mark dividend for the previous year.  </p>
<p>The company, a unit of Walter-Bau-Gruppe, also said in a statement it wanted to add 18.4 million marks from its 1996 profits to its reserves.</p>
<p>A company spokesman declined to say what the company's profits for 1996 would be, saying this would be announced at a news conference on May 15.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, +49 228 26097160</p>
